            <title>0.9.8</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:51:04 +1300</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>9</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Move files and folders on your iPhone or iPad (Pro)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Drag files and folders onto a folder, onto the path bar, or onto the app in the sidebar to move them within that app. Folders spring open as you hover.</li>
<li>Or choose File › Move To…, or copy with ⌘C and choose Edit › Move Item Here (⌥⌘V).</li>
<li>If something with the same name is already there, choose Skip, Replace or Keep Both. Folders with the same name are merged.</li>
<li>Undo and Redo work for moves, several steps back.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Folder sizes</h3>
<ul>
<li>In list view, the Size column shows each folder’s total, including everything in its subfolders, the way Finder counts.</li>
<li>Sorting by size now sorts folders by their totals.</li>
<li>Sizes appear as they’re counted. Small folders show theirs straight away, even next to a folder with tens of thousands of photos.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Faster</h3>
<ul>
<li>Apps open instantly. Opening an app’s files, previewing and copying no longer wait about a second the first time.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Files stored in iCloud</h3>
<ul>
<li>A Mac file that’s only in iCloud Drive (with “Optimise Mac Storage” on) is now downloaded first, then copied to your device. Before, the copy could freeze on it.</li>
<li>While a file downloads, the copy says “downloading from iCloud”, with a percentage when there is one. Cancel stops it straight away.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Shuttle Mode</h3>
<ul>
<li>The transfer speed now shows in the menu bar by default. If you turned it off, it stays off. Change it in Settings › Shuttle Mode › Show speed in menu bar.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Welcome tour</h3>
<ul>
<li>The Connect step is shorter and clearer, and shows what Shuttle Mode looks like during a transfer.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
